    {
      "command": "router-agent --help\n",
      "stdout": "usage: router-agent [-h] [--version]\n                    {auth,capabilities,status,get,traffic,clients,snapshot,diff,plan,plan-show,approval-request,apply,verify,rollback} ...\n\nBounded router evidence; native compatibility is unverified.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {auth,capabilities,status,get,traffic,clients,snapshot,diff,plan,plan-show,approval-request,apply,verify,rollback}\n    auth                User-operated desktop Secret Service onboarding\n    capabilities        Offline inventory; does not establish firmware support\n    status              Read identity, WAN, CPU and RAM\n    get                 Read selected named telemetry groups\n    traffic             Selected native rates for fresh aliased nodes\n    clients             Read and page aliased clients\n    snapshot            Save status or list local snapshots\n    diff                Compare two local snapshots\n    plan                Preview a native change\n    plan-show           Inspect a stored local plan without router requests\n    approval-request    Print exact scope for a separate administrator\n                        approval window\n    apply               Apply with an administrator window and human\n                        confirmation over HTTPS; a no-op sends zero writes,\n                        but performs reads\n    verify              Read current state to verify a stored plan\n    rollback            Preview a reverse plan; separate confirmation and\n                        apply are required\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --version             show program's version number and exit\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "exit_code": 0
    },
    {
